      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The abandoned Valmont train depot, built in 1890, once served the Union Pacific Railroad's Boulder Branch at milepost 24.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valmont%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The old Valmont School, replaced in 1911, closed in 1951 and has been vacant since the 1980s, now owned by local business owners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valmont%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Valmont sits east of Boulder, bordered by Boulder Creek to the north and the 200‑foot‑tall Valmont Butte to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valmont%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2018, the City of Boulder acquired the former Poor Farm/Fort Chambers property, now being developed with the theme “Heal the Land; Heal the People.”.",
